# ──────────────────────── Runtime / data ────────────────────────
# ANCHOR runtime paths (leading slash / explicit prefix). An unanchored `data/`,
# `uploads/` or `*.db` matches at ANY depth, and git on Windows compares ignore
# patterns case-insensitively (core.ignorecase=true) — so `*.db` silently swallowed
# the entire Outcome.Identity.Db + Outcome.Chat.Db projects and `uploads/` swallowed
# Outcome.Chat.Core/Uploads/. All three were missing from the repo; a fresh clone
# could not build. Keep new runtime rules anchored so they can't eat source folders.
/data/
/uploads/
Server/uploads/   # legacy Go backend's on-disk file store (superseded by MinIO)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Belt-and-braces for the `*.db` file rule above: the trailing slash scopes this
# negation to DIRECTORIES, so *.Db projects are tracked while real SQLite files
# (and Thumbs.db) stay ignored. The directory itself must be un-ignored — git never
# descends into an excluded directory, so re-including files inside one is impossible.
!*.Db/
*.pem
acme_certs/

# ──────────────────────── Secrets / local env ───────────────────
.env
.env.local
*.local.yaml
appsettings.Development.local.json

# ──────────────────────────── OS / editor ───────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# Claude Code personal settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Mail server state (account hashes + DKIM private keys) lives on the server only
deploy/compose/mail-config/

# Third-party crypto payment gateway (GPL-3.0), vendored for reference — kept OUT of this
# proprietary tree on purpose. It runs as a separate service, never linked into our code.
/tokenpay/

# Apple signing/push keys — secrets, never in the repo (kept in ~/.outcome/)
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# Desktop shell build output
desktop/node_modules/
desktop/web/
desktop/release/
